# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules.
# Consumed as config by the assets runtime — never served as a file.
# Rules cascade: /* applies everywhere, more specific paths add to it.
#
# CSP notes:
#  - The script-src sha256 is the inline theme-bootstrap script that runs before
#    first paint to prevent a flash of the wrong theme. It is byte-identical in
#    index.html and docs/index.html, so one hash covers both. EDITING THAT SCRIPT
#    INVALIDATES THE HASH and the theme flash returns — regenerate with the
#    command in README.md ("Response headers") and update this line.
#  - <script type="application/ld+json"> blocks need no hash: browsers never
#    execute non-JS MIME types, so script-src does not apply to them.
#  - style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' only because 42 inline style="" attributes
#    remain site-wide. There are no inline <style> blocks. Move those 42 into
#    styles.css and this can tighten to 'self'. websitePages.test.ts pins the count
#    and ratchets it down — never raise its budget to make a new page pass.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-m1EaAXpDarTf/8ASCyWPa6/ZDODIJgodhhLFdCZAbT0='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Vendor connector logos and the favicon: effectively static, safe to pin hard.
/db-icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Subsetted Geist woff2 — content-stable, never edited in place, and
# geist-latin.woff2 is preloaded on every page. Same treatment as /db-icons/*.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Docs screenshots are regenerated at release time under the SAME filenames
# (e2e/screenshots/capture.ts), so `immutable` would strand viewers on a stale
# image for a year. A week keeps the win without outliving the release cadence.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# Unhashed filenames — any site edit changes these in place, so they get a short
# fresh window and then revalidate. Still removes the per-navigation round-trip.
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
